-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/033156ff-5711-4a0c-9a31-cc7a9a10bf7e
-- title:
--   Helmholtz equation, reflectionless ansatz, permittivity profile and physical conditions (i)-(v)
-- statement:
--   Objects of Philbin, *All-frequency reflectionlessness* (2015), PDF pp. 3-5. Throughout, $c>0$ is the speed of light and $k_0=\omega/c$.
--
--   1. **Helmholtz equation (eq. 1).** At normal incidence and real frequency $\omega$, a field $E(x)$ in a planar non-magnetic medium of permittivity $\varepsilon(x,\omega)$ satisfies $E''(x)+k_0^2\,\varepsilon(x,\omega)E(x)=0$. A solution at $x$ is twice differentiable there.
--   2. **Ansatz (eq. 2).** For a complex function $P(x,\omega)$ and a constant $E_0$, $E(x,\omega)=E_0\exp\big[ik_0\int_0^xP(x',\omega)\,dx'\big]$.
--   3. **Generated permittivity (eq. 3).** $\varepsilon(x,\omega)=P(x,\omega)^2-\dfrac{ic}{\omega}\,\partial_xP(x,\omega)$, for complex $\omega\ne0$.
--   4. **Choice of $P$ (eq. 4) and profile (eq. 8).** $P(x,\omega)=1+\dfrac{f(x)}{(\gamma-i\omega)^2}$ with real $f$ and $\gamma>0$. The example takes $f(x)=\dfrac{\Omega^2}{2}\big[1+\tanh(-x/a)\big]$, $a>0$. The far-left limit of this $P$ is $n_-(\omega)=1+\Omega^2/(\gamma-i\omega)^2$.
--   5. **Physical conditions (i)-(v) on $\varepsilon$.**
--      (i) for every $x$, $\varepsilon(x,\cdot)$ is analytic in the open upper half-plane and continuous on the closed upper half-plane minus $\omega=0$;
--      (ii) $\varepsilon(x,-\omega)=\overline{\varepsilon(x,\omega)}$ for real $\omega\ne0$;
--      (iii) $\operatorname{Im}\varepsilon(x,\omega)>0$ for real $\omega>0$;
--      (iv) for some integer $n\ge-1$ and every $x$ there are $a(x),b(x)$ with $\varepsilon(x,\omega)=a(x)+b(x)\omega^n+o(\omega^n)$ as real $\omega\to0$; the relaxed version allowing a $1/\omega^2$ divergence takes $n\ge-2$;
--      (v) for every $x$ there is $C(x)$ with $\varepsilon(x,\omega)=1+C(x)/\omega^2+o(\omega^{-2})$ as real $\omega\to\infty$.
--   6. **Mirrored slab (Fig. 2).** Cutting $\varepsilon$ at $x_0$ and attaching its mirror image gives $\varepsilon_s(x)=\varepsilon(x)$ for $x\ge x_0$ and $\varepsilon(2x_0-x)$ for $x<x_0$. The field of a plane source at the cut is $E_s(x)=E(x)$ for $x\ge x_0$ and $E(2x_0-x)$ for $x<x_0$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The paper writes conditions (iv) and (v) with "$\sim$". They are read as asymptotic expansions with $o$-remainders, and the frequency limits are taken along real $\omega$. In (i), continuity up to the real axis is added so that the real-frequency values are the boundary values of the analytic function, which is what the Kramers–Kronig relations require. Formula (3) is defined for every complex $\omega$, but it is used only for $\omega\ne0$.
-- source:
--   T. G. Philbin, All-frequency reflectionlessness, arXiv:1510.02920v1 (2015), unnumbered main text: conditions (i)-(v), eqs. (1)-(4), (8), PDF pp. 3-4; mirrored slab, final paragraph, PDF p. 5

import Mathlib

/-!
T. G. Philbin, *All-frequency reflectionlessness*, arXiv:1510.02920v1 (2015): the scalar Helmholtz
equation (1) at normal incidence, the field ansatz (2), the permittivity (3) it generates, the
choice (4) of `P`, the profile (8), the physical conditions (i)-(v) on a permittivity, and the
mirrored slab of the final paragraph (PDF pp. 3-5). The letter has no section numbers.
-/

open Filter Topology Asymptotics

noncomputable section

namespace Arxiv1510_02920

/-- Eq. (2), PDF p. 3: the field `E(x,ω) = E₀ exp[i k₀ ∫₀ˣ P(x',ω) dx']` with `k₀ = ω/c`, at a
real frequency `ω`. `P` is a complex function of position and (complex) frequency. -/
def waveField (c : ℝ) (E0 : ℂ) (P : ℝ → ℂ → ℂ) (ω : ℝ) (x : ℝ) : ℂ :=
  E0 * Complex.exp (Complex.I * ((ω / c : ℝ) : ℂ) * ∫ t in (0 : ℝ)..x, P t (ω : ℂ))

/-- Eq. (1), PDF p. 3: the function `E` solves the scalar Helmholtz equation
`[d²/dx² + k₀² ε(x,ω)] E = 0`, `k₀ = ω/c`, at the point `x`, where `ε = eps` is the permittivity
at the fixed real frequency `ω`. `E` is required to be differentiable near `x` and `E'` to be
differentiable at `x`, so that `E''(x)` is a genuine second derivative. -/
def HelmholtzAt (c ω : ℝ) (eps E : ℝ → ℂ) (x : ℝ) : Prop :=
  (∀ᶠ y in 𝓝 x, DifferentiableAt ℝ E y) ∧ DifferentiableAt ℝ (deriv E) x ∧
    deriv (deriv E) x + ((ω / c : ℝ) : ℂ) ^ 2 * eps x * E x = 0

/-- Eq. (3), PDF p. 3: the permittivity generated by the ansatz (2),
`ε(x,ω) = P(x,ω)² − (i c/ω) ∂ₓP(x,ω)`, for complex frequency `ω ≠ 0`. -/
def perm (c : ℝ) (P : ℝ → ℂ → ℂ) (x : ℝ) (ω : ℂ) : ℂ :=
  P x ω ^ 2 - Complex.I * (c : ℂ) / ω * deriv (fun y : ℝ => P y ω) x

/-- Eq. (4), PDF p. 3: `P(x,ω) = 1 + f(x)/(γ − iω)²` with a real function `f` and `γ > 0`. -/
def ansatzP (f : ℝ → ℝ) (γ : ℝ) (x : ℝ) (ω : ℂ) : ℂ :=
  1 + (f x : ℂ) / ((γ : ℂ) - Complex.I * ω) ^ 2

/-- Eq. (8), PDF p. 3: the profile `f(x) = (Ω²/2)[1 + tanh(−x/a)]`, `a > 0`. -/
def tanhProfile (Om a : ℝ) (x : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  Om ^ 2 / 2 * (1 + Real.tanh (-x / a))

/-- Eqs. (4) and (8), PDF p. 3: the function `P` of the paper's example,
`P(x,ω) = 1 + f(x)/(γ − iω)²` with `f` the profile (8). -/
def tanhP (Om a γ : ℝ) : ℝ → ℂ → ℂ :=
  ansatzP (tanhProfile Om a) γ

/-- Eqs. (3), (4) and (8), PDF pp. 3-4 (plotted in Fig. 1): the permittivity of the paper's
example, `ε = P² − (ic/ω) ∂ₓP` with `P` from (4) and `f` from (8). -/
def tanhPerm (c Om a γ : ℝ) : ℝ → ℂ → ℂ :=
  perm c (tanhP Om a γ)

/-- PDF p. 4, paragraph after Fig. 1: the limit `1 + Ω²/(γ − iω)²` of `P(x,ω)` as `x → −∞` for
the example (4), (8); the far-left homogeneous material has permittivity equal to its square. -/
def mediumIndex (Om γ : ℝ) (ω : ℂ) : ℂ :=
  1 + ((Om ^ 2 : ℝ) : ℂ) / ((γ : ℂ) - Complex.I * ω) ^ 2

/-- Condition (i), PDF p. 3: for every `x`, `ε(x,·)` is analytic in the open upper half of the
complex `ω`-plane. It is also required to be continuous on the closed upper half-plane minus
`ω = 0`, so that its values at real `ω` are the boundary values of the analytic function (the
reading needed for the Kramers–Kronig relations the paper invokes). -/
def CondAnalytic (eps : ℝ → ℂ → ℂ) : Prop :=
  ∀ x, AnalyticOnNhd ℂ (eps x) {w : ℂ | 0 < w.im} ∧
    ContinuousOn (eps x) {w : ℂ | 0 ≤ w.im ∧ w ≠ 0}

/-- Condition (ii), PDF p. 3: `ε(x,−ω) = ε*(x,ω)` for every `x` and every real `ω ≠ 0`. -/
def CondReality (eps : ℝ → ℂ → ℂ) : Prop :=
  ∀ (x ω : ℝ), ω ≠ 0 → eps x (-(ω : ℂ)) = star (eps x (ω : ℂ))

/-- Condition (iii), PDF p. 3 (no gain): `Im ε(x,ω) > 0` for every `x` and every real `ω > 0`. -/
def CondNoGain (eps : ℝ → ℂ → ℂ) : Prop :=
  ∀ (x ω : ℝ), 0 < ω → 0 < (eps x (ω : ℂ)).im

/-- Condition (iv), PDF p. 3, with lowest allowed exponent `nmin` (the paper's (iv) is
`nmin = -1`; the relaxed condition of PDF p. 5 allowing a `1/ω²` divergence is `nmin = -2`):
there is an integer `n ≥ nmin` such that for every `x`,
`ε(x,ω) = a(x) + b(x) ωⁿ + o(ωⁿ)` as real `ω → 0`, `ω ≠ 0`. -/
def CondLowFreq (nmin : ℤ) (eps : ℝ → ℂ → ℂ) : Prop :=
  ∃ n : ℤ, nmin ≤ n ∧ ∀ x, ∃ a b : ℂ,
    (fun ω : ℝ => eps x (ω : ℂ) - (a + b * (ω : ℂ) ^ n)) =o[𝓝[≠] (0 : ℝ)]
      (fun ω : ℝ => (ω : ℂ) ^ n)

/-- Condition (v), PDF p. 3: for every `x`, `ε(x,ω) = 1 + C(x)/ω² + o(1/ω²)` as real `ω → ∞`. -/
def CondHighFreq (eps : ℝ → ℂ → ℂ) : Prop :=
  ∀ x, ∃ C : ℂ,
    (fun ω : ℝ => eps x (ω : ℂ) - (1 + C / (ω : ℂ) ^ 2)) =o[atTop]
      (fun ω : ℝ => 1 / (ω : ℂ) ^ 2)

/-- PDF p. 5, final paragraph (Fig. 2): the slab obtained by cutting the permittivity `eps` at
`x = x₀` and attaching its mirror image in the plane of the cut: `eps(x)` for `x ≥ x₀` and
`eps(2x₀ − x)` for `x < x₀`. -/
def slabPerm (eps : ℝ → ℂ → ℂ) (x0 : ℝ) (x : ℝ) (ω : ℂ) : ℂ :=
  if x0 ≤ x then eps x ω else eps (2 * x0 - x) ω

/-- PDF p. 5, final paragraph (Fig. 2): the field of a plane source at the cut `x₀` of the
mirrored slab, equal to the exiting wave `E` for `x ≥ x₀` and to its mirror image `E(2x₀ − x)`
for `x < x₀`. -/
def slabField (E : ℝ → ℂ) (x0 : ℝ) (x : ℝ) : ℂ :=
  if x0 ≤ x then E x else E (2 * x0 - x)

end Arxiv1510_02920


